extraction_notes: |
  - Pages: heading and lore printed 76-78 (cache p077-p079), level-by-level powers printed 78-79, special powers and stat block printed 79 (p080); p081 is art only, and the money paragraph ends on printed 81 (p082). Printed 79 was rendered and matches the text layer; "3D4xlO", "81.S.P." and "!D4xlOO" are the known digit faults for 3D4x10, 8 I.S.P. and 1D4x100.
  - GROUP: the book calls Psi-Warriors knights-errant and notes some join the Cyber-Knights while remaining Psi-Warriors (printed 77), but its stat block is headed "Psi-Warrior Psychic R.C.C." (printed 79) and every power comes from psionic training, so occ_group is psychic (the batch default) rather than men-of-arms. Stored as category occ per the batch''s Mind Melter convention. No S.D.C. or hit point formula is printed (only the +4D6 S.D.C. bonus), so men_of_arms: false.
  - XP: xp_table is the Psi-Warrior ladder read off printed 157.
  - I.S.P.: 3D4x10 + M.E., +8 per additional level (confirmed on the render). Master Psychic, saves vs psionics on 10 or higher (from psionics.type). P.P.E. 2D4.
  - PSIONICS: the Psi-Warrior chooses almost nothing: every power through level 8 is granted by name. Level 1 powers are in psionics.powers; levels 2-8 are powers_schedule entries whose from list equals the count, so the whole list is taken. From level 9 the book says the character "can select one psionic power from either the Healer or Sensitive category"; read as one per level at 9-15 (judgement call, printed 79). categories_allowed is Healing and Sensitive because those are the only free picks.
  - POWER NAMES mapped to catalog rows: Replenish P.P.E. -> Restore P.P.E. (this book''s new power, listed as Restore P.P.E. in its own power list, printed 35); Increase Healing -> Increased Healing; Combat Initiative -> Intuitive Combat (judgement call: no Combat Initiative power exists in this book''s list or the catalog; Intuitive Combat is this book''s new melee-awareness power giving +3 initiative, printed 39); Bio-regeneration (super) -> Bio-Regeneration (Super); Impervious to Poison -> Impervious to Poison/Toxin; Commune with Spirits -> Commune with Spirit; Bio-Manipulation -> Bio-Manipulation (the evil eye); See the Invisible -> See The Invisible.
  - BONUSES: R.C.C. bonuses +1 M.A., +1D6 P.S., +1 P.E., +4D6 S.D.C. (pool bonus), +1 initiative, +1 pull punch, +1 roll, +10% vs coma/death, +2 vs possession at levels 2, 6, 9 and 12, +1 vs Horror Factor at 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13 and 15. The second-level "Art of Defense" bonuses (+1 disarm, +2 pull punch, +1 dodge, +1 roll) are unconditional and stored at level 2. The Psi-Shield parry bonus (levels 2, 6, 9, 12, 15) and the third-level Psi-Sword bonuses (+1 initiative, +2 strike, +1 attack) apply only while that power is in use, so they are special_abilities, not bonuses.
  - SKILLS: bases are catalog base plus printed bonus. The book prints Intelligence (+6%) and Horsemanship: General (+16%); both confirmed on the render and stored as printed. Tracking is the Tracking (people) row. Native Tongue at 98% added per batch convention alongside the two Languages of choice (+20%). The one ancient and two modern W.P.s cannot be split by era in the catalog; both are Weapon Proficiencies choices with notes. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts is granted outright and the page prints no upgrade price, so no hand_to_hand cost block.
  - RELATED: five, plus one at 3, 6, 9 and 12. Science "Math only" is Mathematics: Basic and Advanced. Cowboy''s "Breaking/Taming Wild Horses" is the Breaking/Taming Wild Horse row. Horsemanship is offered beside Pilot: Any because the catalog files riding skills in their own category (judgement call, as the other drafts in this batch). Secondary: two at levels 1, 4 and 8.
  - EQUIPMENT: armor choice enumerates Crusader and Gladiator (the book''s favorites) plus common light suits. "Matches and a lighter" is the matches row plus disposable-lighter. 100 feet of rope is five 20-foot rope rows. Handcuffs are handcuffs-regular (1D4 pairs). 1D4+1 weeks of emergency rations is stored as 1D4+1 emergency-food-rations. "Wood cross" is wooden-cross. The ancient and modern weapon choices enumerate catalog rows; three extra E-clips for each modern weapon is six E-clips. Good quality horse is riding-horse. The note that they favor magic and Techno-Wizard weapons is not stored.
  - MONEY: 2D4x100 Universal credits stored; 1D4x100 worth of salable items is not coin and is not stored. The book adds (printed 80) that merchants often give Psi-Warriors 10-25% discounts; see GM Notes.
  - NOT STORED: alignment (any, leaning scrupulous, unprincipled and aberrant); attribute requirements (none; high I.Q., M.E., P.S. and P.P. helpful); race frequency (humans 68%, Elves 10%, Ogres 5%, others 17%; male or female). No race restriction is stored - humans are the most common Psi-Warriors.
---

## Lore

Legend credits the long-lost kingdom of Psyscape with creating the Psi-Warrior, a training regimen that turned psychics with physical, "reactive" powers into champions against supernatural invaders. Whether or not that is true, today''s Psi-Warriors are volunteers trained either at the village of Potomkane in the old Ohio ruins or at Xanatoa, a monastery of seers in a pocket dimension resembling medieval China; both schools teach the same discipline of mind and body, respect for life, and hatred of supernatural evil and of those who abuse psionics or magic. Candidates endure a year of selection followed by years of martial, spiritual and psionic study, with their powers unlocked gradually. Graduates belong to no order and are sent out to find their own place; most become wandering champions, community defenders or monster hunters, though a minority turn their skills to selfish or evil ends. They disdain politics and their abilities keep growing as they gain experience.

## GM Notes

**A ladder, not a menu.** The Psi-Warrior''s powers arrive in fixed packages - Defense at 2nd level, Offense (including the Psi-Sword) at 3rd, the Mind''s Eye at 4th, and so on through the Dedicated Warrior at 8th. Only from 9th level does the character choose, one Healing or Sensitive power per level.

**Psi-Shield and Psi-Sword.** The shield''s parry bonus (+1 at levels 2, 6, 9, 12 and 15) and the ability to parry projectiles and energy blasts at -3 (P.P. bonus only) apply only while the shield is up. The sword''s +1 initiative, +2 strike and extra melee attack apply only while the sword is in hand. Add them at the table.

**Deprivation.** The character can go two days per level without water and three days per level without food, and four days without sleep, but after three days suffers -5% speed and skills, -1 initiative, -1 parry and dodge and -1 punch/kick damage, repeated every two days thereafter.

**Ley lines.** Duration and range of powers +50% within a mile of a ley line; duration, range and damage double within a mile of a nexus.

**Reputation.** Merchants and vendors often give Psi-Warriors 10% to 25% off goods and services. Many Psi-Warriors give away much of their money to the needy.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-warrior';

